<title>UK: Total aluminium stocks fall in May - IPAI.</title>
<headline>Total aluminium stocks fall in May - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total stocks of all forms of aluminium at Western world smelters excluding finished end-products, fell to 3.045 million tonnes at the end of May 1997, compared with 3.047 million in April and 3.404 million in May 1996, provisional International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) figures show.</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks rose to 1.549 million tonnes versus 1.536 million and 1.859 million, respectively.  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of the total aluminium stocks was as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			    May'97   Apr'97    May'96</p>
<p>    Africa		    61	 62	  83</p>
<p>    North America	1,421    1,436     1,629</p>
<p>    Latin America	  136	149	 180</p>
<p>    Asia		     151	148	 175</p>
<p>    Europe		 1,141    1,119     1,201</p>
<p>    Oceania		  135	133	 136</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks were distributed as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			   May'97    Apr'97    May'96</p>
<p>    Africa		    24	 24	  37</p>
<p>    North America	  595	610	 761</p>
<p>    Latin America	   87	 99	 131</p>
<p>    Asia		     113	109	 150</p>
<p>    Europe		   639	604	 676</p>
<p>    Oceania		   91	 90	 104</p>
</text>
